(N'Maria', N'Bell', N'maria.bell2439@example.org', '2016-02-09', 5, N'Great replacement for our old ones'),
(N'Jonathan', N'Nowak', N'jonathan.nowak9883@example.net', '2016-02-09', 5, N'The end of potentially one of the greatest Naruto game series ever made! Having watched Naruto since its inception, read the Manga pretty much since it first appeared in Shonen Jump, as well as played several iterations of Naruto video games, including the entire Naruto Ninja Storm Series, I can say that this game series is a gem among gems. For perhaps even the most casual Naruto fan, these games actually attempt (and quite successfully I might add) to retell the main story-line from the show, and now with this final iteration, we have officially reached the end of Naruto and Naruto Shippuden respectively. Mechanics wise, this game is the same as prior iterations in the series, save for a few improvements to both the Ai, added battle mechanics, and even the types of battles added during the story. So even if you have held off from other iterations in the series or skipped one or two along the line, you should be able to pick of the game right from the get go. Probably (IMO) the...'),
(N'Anthony', N'Taylor', N'anthony.taylor8471@example.com', '2016-02-10', 2, N'One of my "new" sticks didn''t even have any of the grip on it it. Junk.'),
(N'Emily', N'Cox', N'emily.cox7180@example.net', '2016-02-10', 3, N'my carrier lost the game in my country :('),
